## Project structure (Screenplay pattern)

```text
tests/<area>/              test cases - only tasks and assertions
resources/tasks/           business actions (keywords with meaningful names and arguments)
resources/assertions/      business checks
resources/interactions/    technical helper keywords - the only place with library keywords (tag "interaction")
resources/pages/           page objects: selectors per page, names PAGE_ELEMENT
resources/abilities/       per library: library import and settings, no keywords
resources/main.resource    standard libraries, CryptoLibrary, addresses and credentials per environment
robot.toml                 profiles for running the tests
```

Every layer only uses the layer below. Tasks **act**, assertions **check** - never mix them. Keywords in
`resources/interactions/` carry the tag `interaction` (`Keyword Tags` in the file) and are never used
directly in tests. All imports start with `${EXECDIR}/` (project folder), never `../` or `${CURDIR}`.

## Commands

| Purpose | Command |
|---------|---------|
| All tests (environment dev) | `uv run robotcode robot` |
| Against another environment | `uv run robotcode -p test robot` |
| Only core tests | `uv run robotcode -p test -p smoke robot` |
| Only check syntax | `uv run robotcode -p check robot` |
| Format and check files | `uv run robocop format`, `uv run robocop check` |
| Encrypt a password | `uv run CryptoLibrary` |
{%- if include_web or include_accessibility %}
| Visible and slower browser | `uv run robotcode -p headed robot` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_desktop %}
| Desktop tests | `uv run robotcode -p desktop robot` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_mobile %}
| Mobile tests | `uv run robotcode -p mobile robot` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_email %}
| E-mail tests | `uv run robotcode -p email robot` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_database and database_driver != 'sqlite' %}
| Own database | `uv run robotcode -p database robot` |
{%- endif %}
{%- if include_sap %}
| SAP tests | `uv run robotcode -p sap robot` |
{%- endif %}

Execution options live only in `robot.toml` (profiles) - never pass them to `robot` directly.

## What you never do

- Ask for passwords, tokens or real personal data, or write them into code.
  Passwords are encrypted with `uv run CryptoLibrary` and only stored as `crypt:…`.
- Weaken tests to make them pass. A bug in the application is a finding, not a test problem.
- Change settings in `resources/main.resource`, `robot.toml` or `pyproject.toml` without pointing it out.
- Change data in the environment `prod`.
